# Active multi-session plan pointer
#
# This file is read by the autonomy loop's iteration prompt (see
# .claude/scripts/autonomy-loop.sh) and by a fresh-context Claude that
# typed `continue` after `/clear`. Both paths must work.
#
# STRUCTURE — the work is two-level:
#   master_plan     the top-level feature backlog (the feature sweep). Its
#                   bug ledger is the master to-do list; remediation clusters
#                   become focused sub-plans.
#   active_subplan  the focused sub-plan the loop is currently working,
#                   phase by phase. The loop only touches the master when the
#                   active sub-plan has no `pending` rows left (see the loop's
#                   ROLL-UP rule — conservative: it advances only to an
#                   EXISTING sibling sub-plan with pending work, never scaffolds
#                   a new one autonomously).
#
# When the active sub-plan changes:
#   1. Update active_subplan below (the loop also rewrites this on roll-up).
#   2. Update the LOG_DIR + "Currently active" comment in
#      .claude/scripts/autonomy-loop.sh if the log bucket should change.
#   3. Commit together.
#
# When the active sub-plan's phases are all `done`/`blocked`: the loop rolls
# up to the master and either advances to a sibling sub-plan (<<SUBPLAN_ADVANCED>>)
# or, if none has pending work, emits <<MASTER_EXHAUSTED>> and surfaces to a
# human to scaffold the next sub-plan. <<ALL_DONE>> only when the master
# backlog is fully remediated.

